---
layout: base.njk
title: About
description: A technologist, social enterprise advocate and curious traveller.
permalink: /about/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{% set quiet = haikus | byId(about.epigraph) %}
<article class="about">
  <p class="folio"><span class="folio-site">{{ site.title }}</span><span class="folio-num">About</span></p>

  <div class="about-hero">
    {% haikuImage about.hero, "(min-width: 60em) 52rem, calc(100vw - 4rem)", true %}
    <p class="about-tagline">{{ about.tagline }}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="about-columns">
    <div class="about-main">
      <h1 class="poem-title">About</h1>
      {% if quiet %}
      <blockquote class="epigraph">
        <div class="poem" lang="{{ quiet.language }}">{% for line in quiet.lines %}<span class="line">{{ line }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>
        <p class="epigraph-credit">from <a href="{{ quiet.url }}">{{ quiet.title }}</a></p>
      </blockquote>
      {% endif %}
      <p class="about-intro">{{ about.intro }}</p>
      <p>Drawn to the simple things in life — open roads, unfamiliar places, good food, the unusual and the unexpected.</p>
      <p>I enjoy conversations with people from all walks of life. Everyone has a story, and sometimes the most memorable encounters are the unplanned ones. A shared meal, a moment in sport, a passing conversation, a different perspective or simply a laugh along the way.</p>
      <p>These are my small memoirs. Moments experienced, sometimes fleeting, sometimes memorable, captured in a few lines and a sketch.</p>
      <p class="signature">{% include "emblem.svg.njk" %}<span class="signature-name">{{ site.author }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <aside class="about-aside" aria-label="Author">
      {% haikuThumb about.portrait, "100px", [200] %}
      <p class="about-name">{{ site.author }}</p>
      <p class="about-bio">Technologist, advocate, traveller. Curious about people, places, food and life.</p>
      <p class="about-links"><a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">Write to me</a> · <a href="/feed.xml">Feed</a></p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="licence" id="licence">
    <h2>Licence and permissions</h2>
    <p>The haiku on this site are © {{ site.author }} and licensed under the
    <a href="{{ site.license.url }}" rel="license">{{ site.license.name }}</a> ({{ site.license.short }}).</p>
    <p>You may copy and share any poem unchanged for non-commercial purposes, as long as you credit
    <strong>{{ site.author }}</strong> and link to <a href="{{ site.url }}">haikutravels.xyz</a>. You may not sell the poems,
    include them in commercial publications, products or services, or publish adaptations or translations
    without permission.</p>
    <p>Commercial use, adaptations and translations can be licensed separately, including on a fee or royalty basis.
    Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>.</p>
    <p class="fine">Sketches and photographs are © {{ site.author }} unless a caption says otherwise and are not covered by the poems' licence.</p>
  </section>
</article>
<script src="/js/lightbox.js?v={{ assets.lightbox }}" defer></script>
